# water_river.fmat — moving water. On a generated river's ribbons
# (ground_edit's rivers, docs/terrain-paint/PHASE_W3.md) `flow_map` steers the
# ripples and the foam by the ribbon's own flow map — downstream, faster in
# narrows and riffles, foam streaming off riffles, boulders and falls — so
# flow_direction and flow_speed are not used there. On a plain face (no
# vertex colours) it drifts along flow_direction as before.
#
# The colour (phase W3's fixes): a little silt and algae, so the shallows show
# the gravel bed going green-brown and the deep runs a dark green-grey rather
# than black; the reflection tinted warm and the roughness up, so a choppy
# reach under a blue sky does not read as a sheet of pure sky blue.
kind: surface
texture: water
doc: 'A flowing river: flow-mapped ripples and foam on a generated river, a little silt and algae.'
effects:
  - effect: water
    absorption: 0.7
    shallow_color: {r: 0.66, g: 0.78, b: 0.64}
    scatter_color: {r: 0.09, g: 0.145, b: 0.105}
    subsurface: 0.4
    roughness: 0.16
    refraction: 0.45
    reflectivity: 0.34
    reflect_color: {r: 0.92, g: 0.96, b: 0.76}
    foam: 1
    caustics: 0.5
    flow_speed: 1.4
    flow_direction: [1, 0]
    flow_map: 1
    detail_scale: 2.2
    detail_strength: 1.3
    wave_amplitude: 0.02
    wave_length: 1.5
    wave_speed: 0.8
